# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# Deleting a file from the repo does NOT remove it from Cloudflare Pages.
# An asset that was served by an earlier deployment stays reachable at its
# old URL, with HTTP 200, no matter how many times it is deleted afterwards.
# Caught on 2026-09-22: fonts/noto-ethiopic.woff2 was removed and every
# reference to it deleted, and it was STILL being served — 198,324 bytes,
# byte-identical to the version in git history.
#
# It is not a correctness problem for visitors (style.css points at the new
# 45.5 KB subset, so no browser asks for the old one) but it is a real one:
# 198 KB of dead weight publicly served and crawlable forever, and a stale
# font is exactly the kind of thing that resurfaces when someone copies the
# old URL out of a cached stylesheet.
#
# The tombstone makes the removal real. `410 Gone` is the correct answer —
# it is permanent and deliberate, unlike 404 which means "never existed".

/fonts/noto-ethiopic.woff2    /404.html   410
